==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|perpetuelly}}; equivalent to {{af|en|perpetual|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pɚˈpɛt͡ʃuəli/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/pəˈpɛtʃʊəli/|/pəˈpɛtjʊəli/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-perpetually.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyph|en|per|pet|u|al|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|?}}

# Seeming to never end; [[endlessly]]; [[constantly]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Chronycle of Englonde|url=https://archive.org/details/chronycleofenglo00word/page/n308/mode/1up|location=[London]|publisher=&lbrack;{{w|Wynkyn de Worde}}&rbrack;|year=[1502]|oclc=1098559298|passage=For whiche offence oure holy fader the pope enioyned hym to make hym to be prayed for '''perpetually'''&nbsp;/ ⁊ lyke as he had done too be taken frome hym his naturall lyfe therfore he ſholde do foũde four tapers to brẽne '''perpetually''' about his body yͭ for yͤ extynccõn of his bodely lyf his ſoule may euer be remẽbred ⁊ lyf in heuẽ in ſpyrytuall lyfe}}
#* {{RQ:Landon Ethel Churchill|pages=268–269|pageref=269|volume=I|passage=Now her work dropped on her knee, and her book fell from her hand; she was '''perpetually''' seeking excuses for change of place; and the change brought added discomfort.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1955|month=January|author=R. S. McNaught|title=From the Severn to the Mersey by Great Western|journal=Railway Magazine|pages=18-19|text=But, like more than one similar North Wales beauty-spot, there had to be (at least at the time of which I write), a quarry, or ironworks, or some kind of industrial plant, which lay '''perpetually''' under a cloud of yellowish smoke—literally a blot on the landscape.}} 

